## Tajweed Colours

Tajweed colours are **standalone constants** in `lib/ui/widgets/tajweed.dart`, matching quran.com's Madani mushaf scheme. They are NOT theme-dependent (same on light and dark).

| Rule | Constant | Colour | Hex |
|------|----------|--------|-----|
| Qalqala (echo) | `kQalqalaColor` | Light Blue | #0091EA |
| Ghunnah / Ikhfa / Idgham-gh / Iqlab / Meem rules | `kGhunnahColor` | Green | #43A047 |
| Normal Madd (2 counts) | `kNormalMaadColor` | Pink | #E91E8C |
| Separated Madd / Aridh (2/4/6) | `kMaadSukoonColor` | Orange | #FB8C00 |
| Connected Madd (4/5, before hamza) | `kMaadConnectedColor` | Dark Pink | #D81B60 |
| Necessary Madd / Lazim (6 counts) | `kMaadLongColor` | Red | #F44336 |
| Silent / not pronounced | `kNotPronouncedColor()` | Grey | #9E9E9E (dark) / #BDBDBD (light) |

`kNotPronouncedColor(Brightness)` is the only brightness-aware colour — returns a different grey for readability on dark vs light backgrounds.

> **Legacy:** `TajweedTheme` (`lib/theme/tajweed_extension.dart`) is still registered in both light and dark `ThemeData` but is **not used** by the tajweed engine. The engine reads colours from the constants above.
